From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] kboot: hand the preloaded AVE encoder firmware over on
 the T8132

iBoot preloads the AVE video encoder firmware on the M4 (T8132) as it does
on the A18 Pro: the J604 ADT /arm-io/ave is "pre-loaded" with a __TEXT and
a __DATA segment range. aura's generic hand-over (ave_compatibles[],
dt_set_ave_node()) already covers the M1, M2, A18 Pro, M4 Pro and M5 Pro
encoders, but not the M4's, so a T8132 encoder node never gets its firmware
regions and the kernel driver stops at "no preloaded firmware".

Add "apple,t8132-ave" to the list, and to the M4-generation encoders whose
firmware keeps running at its remap addresses (use_remap).

On the J604 boot ADT the segments are TEXT 0x148000 bytes at
0x10000b88000 (remap 0x10000000000) and DATA 0x12c000 bytes at
0x10001cd8000 (remap 0x10000148000), both below the OS. The same hand-over
on the omacom m1n1 tree bound the J604 encoder and both its DARTs
(linux-aurora 1.720).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/kboot.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index 2357dcdd..03f21ac0 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -4233,7 +4233,8 @@ static int dt_reserve_asc_firmware(const char *adt_path, const char *adt_path_al
  * it takes.
  */
 static const char *const ave_compatibles[] = {
-    "apple,t6000-ave", "apple,t8112-ave", "apple,t8140-ave", "apple,t6041-ave", "apple,t6050-ave",
+    "apple,t6000-ave", "apple,t8112-ave", "apple,t8132-ave", "apple,t8140-ave", "apple,t6041-ave",
+    "apple,t6050-ave",
 };
 
 /*
@@ -4617,7 +4618,8 @@ static int dt_set_ave_node(int node, const char *compat, u32 phandle)
      * The pre-M4 (6070) firmware runs from DART address zero (the ADT iova-offset); the
      * M4-generation encoders keep running at their remap addresses.
      */
-    bool use_remap = !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, node, "apple,t8140-ave") ||
+    bool use_remap = !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, node, "apple,t8132-ave") ||
+                     !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, node, "apple,t8140-ave") ||
                      !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, node, "apple,t6041-ave") ||
                      !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, node, "apple,t6050-ave");
     /*
